Defects found:

- `line 40` - NEGATION DROPPED / substring match.
  Input: `for text, fields in not_tidy(s.paras): pass\ndef p(s, scope=None):\n    return not_tidy(G.render(canon, s, scope))\n`
  Consequence: `check()` returns pass because `not_tidy(` contains `_tidy(`.

- `line 39` - idempotency guard satisfied by comment/marker.
  Input: `# for text, fields in _tidy(s.paras):\ndef p(s, scope=None):\n    return _tidy(G.render(canon, s, scope))\n`
  Consequence: `check()` passes with no real paragraph render loop.

- `lines 52-53` - selector only sees the first `return` in `p`.
  Input: `for text, fields in _tidy(s.paras): pass\ndef p(s, scope=None):\n    if scope:\n        return _tidy(G.render(canon, s, scope))\n    return G.render(canon, s, scope)\n`
  Consequence: the untidied card-render branch is invisible and `check()` passes.

- `line 61` - off-by-one/topology check does not enforce “exactly once”.
  Input: `for text, fields in _tidy(s.paras): pass\nfor text, fields in _tidy(other.paras): pass\ndef p(s, scope=None):\n    return _tidy(G.render(canon, s, scope))\n`
  Consequence: two paragraph render loops pass despite the stated invariant that there is exactly one.

- `lines 114-117` - selector keyed to one append spelling.
  Input in `build_tabbed.py` or `paper_projector.py`: `s.paras.append ("x")`
  Consequence: the reported append-path count omits a real append site.

